[{"id":"smq-year1-1.43-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>State the period of each of the following functions:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\sin2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\cos6x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\tan x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\sin\\left(\\frac12x\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\cos\\left(\\frac14x\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\tan(2x-45)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\sin\\left(\\frac{360}7x\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\cos\\left(\\frac{90}{13}x+\\frac{360}{13}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\sin\\left(\\frac{72}{73}(x-30)\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\cos(15(x+7))\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ\\div2=180^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ\\div6=60^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"180^\\circ\\div1=180^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ\\div\\frac12=720^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ\\div\\frac14=1440^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"180^\\circ\\div2=90^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">g)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ\\div\\frac{360}7=7^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">h)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ\\div\\frac{90}{13}=52^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">i)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ\\div\\frac{72}{73}=365^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">j)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ\\div15=24^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.43-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>In each of the following cases, the curve</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\sin x\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>has been stretched parallel to the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis. State the equation of each curve.</p><div class=\"math-table\"><table><tr><td><p><strong>a)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.43/questions/diagrams/q2a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></td><td><p><strong>b)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.43/questions/diagrams/q2b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>c)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.43/questions/diagrams/q2c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></td><td><p><strong>d)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.43/questions/diagrams/q2d.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></td></tr></table></div>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin\\left(\\frac{360}{180}x\\right)=\\sin(2x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin\\left(\\frac{360}1x\\right)=\\sin(360x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin\\left(\\frac{360}7x\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin\\left(\\frac{360}{52}x\\right)=\\sin\\left(\\frac{90}{13}x\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.43-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>All the following graphs are transformations of</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\sin x.\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>State the equation of each:</p><div class=\"math-table\"><table><tr><td><p><strong>a)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.43/questions/diagrams/q3a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></td><td><p><strong>b)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.43/questions/diagrams/q3b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>c)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.43/questions/diagrams/q3c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></td><td><p><strong>d)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.43/questions/diagrams/q3d.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></td></tr></table></div>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3\\sin\\left(\\frac{360}7x\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2\\sin\\left(\\frac{360}1x\\right)=2\\sin(360x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=10\\sin\\left(\\frac{360}{20}x\\right)=10\\sin(18x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-5\\sin\\left(\\frac{360}{30}x\\right)=-5\\sin(12x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.43-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>State the amplitude of each of the following periodic functions:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2+\\cos(15x+3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=40+18\\sin(12x-4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3-5\\sin(0.5x+1.1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"18\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.43-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>For each of the following functions state the minimum and maximum of the function:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin3x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=4+\\cos(12x^\\circ-7)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=25+15\\sin(30x+2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3-8\\sin(0.5x+0.2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Max is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, min is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Max is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4+1=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, min is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4-1=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Max is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"25+15=40\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, min is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"25-15=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Max is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3+8=11\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, min is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3-8=-5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.43-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>All the following graphs are of the form</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=a+b\\sin(cx).\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>In each case, find the equation of the graph:</p><div class=\"math-table\"><table><tr><td><p><strong>a)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.43/questions/diagrams/q6a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></td><td><p><strong>b)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.43/questions/diagrams/q6b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>c)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.43/questions/diagrams/q6c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></td><td><p><strong>d)</strong></p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.43/questions/diagrams/q6d.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></td></tr></table></div>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Period: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"360\\div10=36\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Amplitude: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{5-1}2=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Translate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\3\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=3+2\\sin(36x).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Period: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"360\\div30=12\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Amplitude: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{2.5-1.5}2=0.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Translate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\2\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=2+0.5\\sin(12x).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Period: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"360\\div20=18\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Amplitude: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{2--4}2=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Translate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-1+3\\sin(18x).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Period: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"7\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"360\\div7\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Amplitude: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{25-15}2=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> but <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> due to reflection.</p>","<p>Translate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\20\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=20-5\\sin\\left(\\frac{360}7x\\right).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.43-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>The time of sunrise, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hours since midnight for each day <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of a year may be modelled by the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=a+b\\cos x^\\circ.\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>It is known that the latest sunrise is at 8:00 am on January 1<sup>st</sup> and the earliest is at 4:30 am, six months later.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Suggest how the model may be improved.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Max <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, Min <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Amplitude: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{8-4.5}2=1.75\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"8-1.75=6.25\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=6.25+1.75\\cos(x).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Change the period to match the yearly cycle:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=6.25+1.75\\cos\\left(\\frac{360}{365}x\\right).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.43-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>A person's blood pressure, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, oscillates between 120 and 80 with their heartbeat occurring every 1 second.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find a model in the form</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=a+b\\sin kt^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the time that has passed in seconds and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a,b,k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constants.</p></li><li><p>Explain why this model will not always be accurate for predicting blood pressure.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Period: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Max <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"120\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, Min <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"80\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Amplitude: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{120-80}2=20\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"120-20=100\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=100+20\\sin(360t).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Blood pressure will change depending on how much a person is moving.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.43-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>The size of a population, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, of wild mice is recorded over time, and may be modelled by a formula of the form</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"P=20+6\\sin(3t-10)^\\circ,\\qquad0\\leq t\\leq121\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of days since the start of the year. According to the model, find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the number of mice in the population after 5 days have passed.</p></li><li><p>the maximum and minimum number of mice in the population.</p></li><li><p>the days on which the maximum and the minimum number of mice in the population occurs.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"20+6\\sin(3\\times5-10)=20.52293446\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"21\" data-display=\"false\"></span> mice.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"20+6=26\\text{ mice}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"20-6=14\\text{ mice}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3t-10=90\\text{ so }t=\\frac{100}3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Maximum occurs between day 33 and day 34.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3t-10=270\\text{ so }t=\\frac{280}3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Minimum occurs between day 93 and day 94.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.43-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>The profits on the sales of ice cream for a shop, \u00a3<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, may be given by the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"P=55-50\\cos\\left(\\frac{72}{73}(x-45)\\right)^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of days since the 1<sup>st</sup> January. According to the model,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>write down the difference between the largest and smallest values of the profits.</p></li></ol><p>During the 136<sup>th</sup> day of the year, the rate of change of the profits is at its maximum.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>Find the next day when the model predicts the rate of change will be the same.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"55-50=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"55+50=105\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>So difference is \u00a3100.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"360\\div\\frac{72}{73}=365\\text{ days}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So one year / 365 days later / 501 days after 1<sup>st</sup> January.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.43-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>Laiyla is monitoring the height of the tide, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres, in her local harbour. At various points of time, she records the height along with the time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hours after midnight.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.43/questions/diagrams/q11.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Laiyla models the data with the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h=5+1.7\\sin(25t-330)^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of hours since midnight.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the minimum height of the tide predicted by Laiyla's model.</p></li><li><p>Find the maximum number of consecutive hours that Laiyla's model predicts that the height of the tide will exceed 6 metres.</p></li><li><p>Find the second time after midnight at which the tide has a height of 6 metres.</p></li></ol><p>Further along the coast, a second location's tide has the same times for its high and low tides, varying in depth by 3.3 metres. At high tide, it is 2.55 metres less deep than the high tide found by Laiyla's model.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li><p>Make appropriate refinements to Laiyla's equation to create a model for the height of the tide.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5-1.7=3.3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"5+1.7\\sin(25t-330)^\\circ=6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sin(25t-330)^\\circ=\\frac1{1.7}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Find the first value:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"25t-330=\\arcsin\\left(\\frac1{1.7}\\right)=36.03187\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Find the second value:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"180-36.03187\\ldots=143.9681209\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"25t-330=144.0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"25t-330=36.03187\\ldots\\Rightarrow t=14.641275\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"25t-330=143.9681209\\ldots\\Rightarrow t=18.9587\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Difference is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4.3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hours.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"18.9587\\ldots-\\frac{360}{25}=4.55872\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4{:}34\" data-display=\"false\"></span> am.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>amplitude is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{3.3}2=1.65\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h=a+1.65\\sin(25t-330)^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>High tide for Laiyla's model: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5+1.7=6.7\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"6.7-2.55=4.15\\text{ metres}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"a+1.65=4.15\\ \\therefore a=2.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore h=2.5+1.65\\sin(25t-330)^\\circ.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]}]